{
  "section": "PR3",
  "title": "Graphs of Polynomial Functions",
  "learningObjective": "Determine the zeros and their multiplicities of a polynomial in factored form. Describe and graph the behavior of a polynomial function at the intercepts and the ends.",
  "faqs": [
    {
      "id": "faq-1",
      "category": "conceptual",
      "question": "What are the \"zeros\" of a polynomial function, and how do I find them from factored form?",
      "answer": "The zeros are the x-values where the function equals 0 — exactly where the graph crosses or touches the x-axis. When a polynomial is already factored, like \\( f(x)=(x-2)(x+1)(x-3)^2 \\), each factor gives a zero directly: set each factor equal to 0 and solve. The Zero Product Property (TE3) is exactly this idea, just applied to a polynomial instead of a trig equation.<div class=\"example-box\"><div class=\"label\">Worked Example</div><p class=\"math-line\">\\( f(x)=(x-2)(x+1)(x-3)^2 \\) has zeros at \\( x=2 \\), \\( x=-1 \\), and \\( x=3 \\) — three distinct zeros total.</p></div>"
    },
    {
      "id": "faq-2",
      "category": "conceptual",
      "question": "What is \"end behavior,\" and why doesn't a polynomial actually have literal ends?",
      "answer": "End behavior describes what the graph does far to the right and far to the left — does it shoot up, or plunge down? A polynomial is actually defined for every single x-value, so it never truly \"ends\"; end behavior is really about the long-run trend as x grows arbitrarily large in either direction.<div class=\"graph-wrap\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 520 440\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\"><line x1=\"16.0\" y1=\"115.0\" x2=\"210.0\" y2=\"115.0\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" /><polyline points=\"28.0,74.0 28.9,76.6 29.7,79.1 30.6,81.6 31.4,83.9 32.3,86.1 33.1,88.3 34.0,90.3 34.8,92.3 35.7,94.2 36.5,96.0 37.4,97.7 38.3,99.4 39.1,101.0 40.0,102.5 40.8,103.9 41.7,105.3 42.5,106.5 43.4,107.8 44.2,108.9 45.1,110.0 45.9,111.1 46.8,112.0 47.6,113.0 48.5,113.8 49.4,114.6 50.2,115.4 51.1,116.1 51.9,116.8 52.8,117.4 53.6,117.9 54.5,118.5 55.3,118.9 56.2,119.4 57.0,119.8 57.9,120.2 58.8,120.5 59.6,120.8 60.5,121.0 61.3,121.2 62.2,121.4 63.0,121.6 63.9,121.7 64.7,121.8 65.6,121.9 66.4,122.0 67.3,122.0 68.2,122.0 69.0,122.0 69.9,122.0 70.7,122.0 71.6,121.9 72.4,121.8 73.3,121.7 74.1,121.6 75.0,121.5 75.8,121.4 76.7,121.2 77.5,121.1 78.4,120.9 79.3,120.7 80.1,120.6 81.0,120.4 81.8,120.2 82.7,120.0 83.5,119.8 84.4,119.6 85.2,119.4 86.1,119.2 86.9,119.0 87.8,118.8 88.7,118.6 89.5,118.3 90.4,118.1 91.2,117.9 92.1,117.7 92.9,117.6 93.8,117.4 94.6,117.2 95.5,117.0 96.3,116.8 97.2,116.6 98.1,116.5 98.9,116.3 99.8,116.2 100.6,116.0 101.5,115.9 102.3,115.8 103.2,115.7 104.0,115.6 104.9,115.5 105.7,115.4 106.6,115.3 107.4,115.2 108.3,115.2 109.2,115.1 110.0,115.1 110.9,115.0 111.7,115.0 112.6,115.0 113.4,115.0 114.3,115.0 115.1,115.0 116.0,115.1 116.8,115.1 117.7,115.2 118.6,115.2 119.4,115.3 120.3,115.4 121.1,115.5 122.0,115.6 122.8,115.7 123.7,115.8 124.5,115.9 125.4,116.0 126.2,116.2 127.1,116.3 127.9,116.5 128.8,116.6 129.7,116.8 130.5,117.0 131.4,117.2 132.2,117.4 133.1,117.6 133.9,117.7 134.8,117.9 135.6,118.1 136.5,118.3 137.3,118.6 138.2,118.