    {
      "id": "faq-3",
      "category": "conceptual",
      "question": "What is multiplicity, and why does it matter for how a graph behaves at a zero?",
      "answer": "Multiplicity is how many times a factor is repeated in the factored form — the exponent on that factor. It matters because it controls the graph's behavior right at that zero: an odd multiplicity means the graph passes straight through, while an even multiplicity means the graph touches the axis and turns back around without crossing.<div class=\"graph-wrap\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 550 260\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\"><line x1=\"10.0\" y1=\"130.0\" x2=\"250.0\" y2=\"130.0\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" /><line x1=\"130.0\" y1=\"40.0\" x2=\"130.0\" y2=\"220.0\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" stroke-dasharray=\"4,3\" /><polyline points=\"20.8,193.0 21.9,192.4 23.0,191.7 24.1,191.1 25.2,190.5 26.3,189.8 27.4,189.2 28.5,188.6 29.6,187.9 30.7,187.3 31.8,186.7 32.9,186.0 34.0,185.4 35.1,184.8 36.2,184.1 37.3,183.5 38.4,182.9 39.5,182.2 40.6,181.6 41.7,181.0 42.7,180.3 43.8,179.7 44.9,179.1 46.0,178.4 47.1,177.8 48.2,177.2 49.3,176.5 50.4,175.9 51.5,175.3 52.6,174.6 53.7,174.0 54.8,173.4 55.9,172.7 57.0,172.1 58.1,171.5 59.2,170.8 60.3,170.2 61.4,169.6 62.5,168.9 63.6,168.3 64.7,167.7 65.8,167.0 66.9,166.4 68.0,165.8 69.1,165.1 70.2,164.5 71.3,163.9 72.4,163.2 73.5,162.6 74.6,162.0 75.7,161.3 76.8,160.7 77.9,160.1 79.0,159.4 80.1,158.8 81.2,158.2 82.3,157.5 83.4,156.9 84.5,156.3 85.6,155.6 86.6,155.0 87.7,154.4 88.8,153.7 89.9,153.1 91.0,152.5 92.1,151.8 93.2,151.2 94.3,150.6 95.4,149.9 96.5,149.3 97.6,148.7 98.7,148.0 99.8,147.4 100.9,146.8 102.0,146.1 103.1,145.5 104.2,144.9 105.3,144.2 106.4,143.6 107.5,143.0 108.6,142.3 109.7,141.7 110.8,141.1 111.9,140.4 113.0,139.8 114.1,139.2 115.2,138.5 116.3,137.9 117.4,137.3 118.5,136.6 119.6,136.0 120.7,135.4 121.8,134.7 122.9,134.1 124.0,133.5 125.1,132.8 126.2,132.2 127.3,131.6 128.4,130.9 129.5,130.3 130.5,129.7 131.6,129.1 132.7,128.4 133.8,127.8 134.9,127.2 136.0,126.5 137.1,125.9 138.2,125.3 139.3,124.6 140.4,124.0 141.5,123.4 142.6,122.7 143.7,122.1 144.8,121.5 145.9