ont-size=\"12.5\" fill=\"#D4622A\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" >x=3: touches, LOCAL MIN</text><rect x=\"4\" y=\"4\" width=\"470\" height=\"210\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4a4a5a\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"240.0\" y=\"26.0\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#4a4a5a\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" >Zoomed in near x = 2 and x = 3</text></svg></div><p class=\"graph-caption\">f(x) = (x−2)(x+1)(x−3)² — the deep dip near x = −0.1 (y ≈ −18.2) dwarfs the small wiggle near the double zero, so that region is shown zoomed in below. Note: x = 3 is a local MINIMUM (the curve touches zero from above), not a maximum.</p>"
